{"id": 60, "ts": 1780629438.0614948, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I respect Sarah\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and calmness, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall fit.\u202fC does keep calm in a crisis and makes quick, correct decisions, and his technical grasp of complex systems is solid. However, the lack of any evidence on his adaptability or willingness to accept feedback\u2014highlighted by his reluctance to pursue further education and the perception of egocentricity\u2014poses a risk for the continuous learning required on long\u2011distance routes.\u202fBy contrast, B\u2019s \u201cvery conscientious\u201d nature directly supports operational reliability, and his proven ability to handle stress, assess weather, and leverage excellent computer skills addresses the core technical and cognitive demands of international flights. The concerns about B\u2014nasty remarks and a weak numeric memory\u2014are behavioral and attentional issues that can be mitigated through targeted coaching and procedural safeguards, whereas C\u2019s communication difficulty and rigidity are deeper cultural fits that are harder to remediate. Given the safety\u2011critical nature of the role, I continue to vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
