{"id": 78, "ts": 1780629607.1580884, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the strongest overall fit.  The discussion has clarified that we still have no concrete evidence of operational reliability for either Candidate\u202fA or Candidate\u202fD, and their teamwork or crew\u2011cooperation profiles are essentially unknown.  In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is documented as\u202f100\u202f% reliable, keeps calm in a crisis, makes correct decisions quickly, understands complicated technology, and creates a positive atmosphere with the crew\u2014covering the core safety\u2011critical criteria of reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, technical competence, and crew cooperation.  While C\u2019s limited willingness to pursue further education and some communication difficulty are noted, these are less immediate safety risks than Candidate\u202fB\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and weak numeric memory, which directly affect crew harmony and attention to detail.  Given the complete lack of reliability evidence for A and D, and the balanced strengths of C, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC."}
