{"id": 98, "ts": 1780629862.8052032, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I respect Sarah\u2019s thorough recap of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s record, especially the 100\u202f% reliability, calmness in crisis, rapid correct decisions, solid technical grasp, and the positive crew atmosphere. Those are indeed strong safety\u2011critical attributes. However, the lack of any evidence on C\u2019s adaptability remains a serious gap \u2013 his reluctance to pursue further education and the perception of egocentricity suggest limited openness to feedback, which is essential for long\u2011distance operations that constantly evolve.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrates concrete reliability (\u201cvery conscientious\u201d), proven stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d), and specific technical competence (accurate weather assessment and \u201cexcellent computer skills\u201d). While B\u2019s \u201cpretentious\u201d tone, occasional \u201cnasty remarks,\u201d and weaker numeric memory are concerns, they are behavioral and attentional issues that can be mitigated through targeted coaching, clear communication protocols, and procedural safeguards.\nGiven that B\u2019s core safety criteria are well\u2011documented and his remaining weaknesses are more remediable than C\u2019s adaptability risk, I maintain my recommendation for Candidate\u202fB."}
